## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design a cohesive, cross-service telemetry story across serverless and containerized workloads, with strict per-tenant isolation and GPU-backed processing. Evaluates practical trade-offs for latency, cost, and reliability in a real-world enterprise scenario.

## Key Concepts

- OpenTelemetry end-to-end trace propagation across HTTP, Event Grid, AKS, Cosmos, and Blob
- Tenant isolation via Cosmos partition keys and tenant-scoped blob namespaces
- GPU-focused AKS autoscaling and queue-driven work orchestration
- Per-tenant budgets and observability with custom autoscaler and metrics
- Event Grid integration with GPU workloads and failure handling

