## Why This Is Asked
Assesses practical knowledge of end-to-end observability in Azure for multi-tenant data pipelines, including cross-service tracing, privacy, and cost considerations.

## Key Concepts
- OpenTelemetry integration with Azure Functions and Event Hubs
- Trace context propagation (tenantId, traceId)
- Azure Monitor / Log Analytics backend for traces
- Per-tenant isolation in logs and data paths
- Dynamic sampling and cost-aware tracing, privacy controls

## Code Example
```javascript
// Node.js (simplified sketch)
const { trace, context, propagation } = require('@opentelemetry/api');
const { registerInstrumentations } = require('@opentelemetry/instrumentation');
const { HttpInstrumentation } = require('@opentelemetry/instrumentation-http');

registerInstrumentations({ instrumentations: [new HttpInstrumentation()], tracerProvider: /*...*/ });

module.exports = async function (context, req) {
  const tenantId = req.headers['x-tenant-id'];
  const span = trace.getTracer('azure-trace').startSpan('function.process', {
    attributes: { tenantId }
  });
  return await context.bindings?.invoke(req, { parent: span.context() });
};
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate dynamic sampling across tenants with different load patterns?
- How would you detect and remediate telemetry leaks that cross tenant boundaries?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of read-through caching, per-tenant data isolation, and latency optimization in a serverless context. It also surfaces familiarity with common Azure data services and simple failure handling.

## Key Concepts
- Read-through caching with Redis in serverless Functions
- Per-tenant data isolation using Table Storage PartitionKey
- TTL strategy to balance freshness and performance
- Cache stampede mitigation and basic error handling

## Code Example
```csharp
// Minimal illustration for GET endpoint
public async Task<IActionResult> GetCatalog(string tenantId, string productId)
{
    var key = $"{tenantId}:{productId}";
    var cached = await _cache.GetStringAsync(key);
    if (cached != null) return new OkObjectResult(JsonConvert.DeserializeObject<Product>(cached));

    var tbl = _table.GetTableReference("Catalog");
    var op = TableOperation.Retrieve<ProductEntity>(tenantId, productId);
    var res = await tbl.ExecuteAsync(op);
    var item = (ProductEntity)res.Result;
    if (item == null) return new NotFoundResult();

    var prod = item.ToProduct();
    await _cache.SetStringAsync(key, JsonConvert.SerializeObject(prod), new DistributedCacheEntryOptions { AbsoluteExpirationRelativeToNow = TimeSpan.FromSeconds(300) });
    return new OkObjectResult(prod);
}
```

